# devices py=['sNULL'] bend=['sCPU'] -- NOT WELL-POSED, and this is NOT a verdict (exit 2). The port's graph fixture is pinned at the arena tag 0 and the py graph is on ['sNULL'], so every consumer of the ALLOC would carry a different `core` and the report would be a cascade of `src` differences with the cause in none of them. Re-run with --dev <the name the port resolved> -- or, if the name is not in the port's table at all, that is a port gap to report, not a flag to set.
